# nr-exthost-doctor-updater: the doctor runtime row and the npm updater no longer take the bundled interpreter

All paths are under native/core/crates/mixdog-app-server-daemon/src. The daemon crate gains no dependency
(the engine name and version are handed in as plain strings).

## compose_flip.rs, the doctor (DoctorInputs, near `doctor: crate::domain_seams::doctor::DaemonDoctorHost::new(`)

Remove the three fields `package_root: b.package_root.clone(),`, `interpreter: ... JsInterpreter { ... },` and
`processes: b.tidy_processes.clone(),` of that `DoctorInputs { ... }` and put, after `data_dir: b.data_dir.clone(),`:

    runtime: crate::domain_seams::doctor::EmbeddedRuntime { name: mixdog_jsrt::ENGINE_NAME.to_owned(), version: mixdog_jsrt::ENGINE_VERSION.to_owned() },

(`mixdog_jsrt` is the crate of nr-exthost-jsrt-engine; the daemon already depends on it by that task's own wire, or this line
adds `mixdog-jsrt = { workspace = true }` to mixdog-app-server-daemon/Cargo.toml.) If those two consts are not `&str`,
convert with `.to_string()`.

## compose_flip.rs, DomainPaths (near `paths: DomainPaths {`)

Delete the two lines `node: b.js_runtime.program.clone(),` and `electron: b.js_runtime.electron,`.

## compose_domains.rs, `pub struct DomainPaths`

Delete the doc comment "The JS interpreter of the install (`JsRuntime::program`) ..." and the fields `pub node: PathBuf,` and
`pub electron: bool,`.

## compose_domains/rows.rs, the `StagedConfig { ... }` built for `StagedInstaller::new`

Delete `node: inputs.paths.node.clone(),` and `electron: inputs.paths.electron,`.

## compose_domains/tests.rs (the DomainPaths literal, near `package_root: js.package_root.clone(),`)

Delete `node: js.program.clone(),` and `electron: js.electron,` of that `DomainPaths { ... }` (the `ExtHostConfig` above it keeps
its own `electron: js.electron`, which belongs to the ext-host tasks).

## What the doctor now shows

The `nodeRuntime` row is `{name, version, engines: null}` (no process is started). The renderer in
mixdog-core-domains diagnostics.rs `report_node` turns `engines: null` into a Warn "v<version> . engine requirement
unavailable"; whoever owns diagnostics.rs decides whether a null `engines` should read as Ok for the embedded engine.

## SERVICE_PENDING

Nothing is removed from it by this task.
